{
"opening": "This release introduces the new TLRU cache algorithm and enhances the key generation utilities with typed method support. It also deprecates legacy caching classes while adding introspection capabilities to decorators.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m01",
"text": "The library must provide a TLRUCache class that implements the Time-LRU eviction policy, exposing standard mapping methods like get, set, pop, and clear. This class should integrate with existing decorator patterns by accepting a timer function to determine item expiration."
},
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "Time-aware cache implementations must ensure that internal time tracking does not alter the signature or behavior of the underlying decorated functions. The expiration logic for these caches must remain consistent regardless of the specific timer implementation provided."
},
{
"id": "m11",
"text": "Cache decorator wrappers must expose their configuration parameters as attributes on the returned function object. This allows external tools to inspect the maxsize, ttl, or other settings used by the cached function without needing to access the internal cache instance directly."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The keys module must export a methodkey function that generates cache keys based on the method name and arguments, excluding the self argument. This complements existing hashkey and typedkey utilities for more robust memoization of class methods."
},
{
"id": "m18",
"text": "Decorators such as @cached and @cachedmethod must provide a cache_clear function that resets the associated cache instance to an empty state. Calling this function should remove all entries and reset any internal statistics counters."
},
{
"id": "m27",
"text": "The @cached decorator must include a cache_info function that returns a named tuple containing cache hit/miss statistics and current size metrics. This information should be accessible without modifying the original function's interface or return value."
},
{
"id": "m65",
"text": "The keys module must provide a typedmethodkey decorator that combines type checking with method-based key generation. This ensures that cached results are distinct based on both the argument types and the method context."
},
{
"id": "m69",
"text": "The MRUCache class and its corresponding @mru_cache decorator must be marked as deprecated in public APIs. Users should receive warnings indicating that these components will be removed in future versions."
},
{
"id": "m71",
"text": "The TTLCache.expire method must return an iterable of (key, value) pairs representing items that have reached their expiration time. This allows consumers to process expired entries before they are automatically removed from the cache."
},
{
"id": "m72",
"text": "The TLRUCache.expire method must return an iterable of (key, value) pairs for items that have exceeded their time-to-live duration. This enables explicit handling of expired data points within the TLRU eviction strategy."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all deprecation warnings are visible during runtime testing and that the new TLRU implementation passes existing compatibility checks."
}
